From eb8074f73f6748a93344cf286133907f5ca4e9cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TrinityXSX <trinityxsx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:04:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] TrinityXSX: benchmark mode (XCL_BENCH_SECONDS)

With XCL_BENCH_SECONDS=N the host waits for the first presented frame,
lets the title run XCL_BENCH_WARMUP seconds (default 15), records N
seconds of present times (PresentX and the vkQueuePresentKHR hook),
writes a JSON summary to XCL_BENCH_OUT (default <logs>/bench.json) and
ends the process: frames, average FPS, p50/p95/p99/max frame time,
1% low FPS, frames over 100 ms, time to the first frame and the peak
commit. A title that shows no frame within 600 s gets "no-frames".
The result's folder is one of XCL's own folders for the VFS, so the
title's write redirection does not move it into the overlay.

The TrinityXSX library's benchmark queue and tools/ps5_bench.py drive
it. Recording costs one atomic load per present when it is off.
